<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo aims to up heavy equipment exports.</title>
<headline>Daewoo aims to up heavy equipment exports.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Corp's trading division said on Monday it aimed to expand heavy equipment exports by 20 percent to $450 million this year.</p>
<p>Daewoo said in a statement it planned to further expand overseas sales of forklift vehicles, excavators and other heavy equipment to $800 million by the year 2000.</p>
<p>To attain the goal, the company plans to strengthen sales activities, especially in Africa and South America and China, the statement added.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
